SupraLINUX integration review for LibKScreen 6.7.5

Preserve signed official upstream sources, Ubuntu epoch 4, both SONAME 8
libraries, six ordinary binary packages, all original symbol guards, SDK,
QCH, translations, D-Bus/systemd helpers and Fake/KWayland/XRandR backends.
Use only exact eligible ECM 6.30.0-0supralinux3 and authoritative supplementary
Plasma Wayland Protocols 1.22.0-0supralinux1, with transport certified before
package execution. Ubuntu Qt 6.10.2, Wayland 1.24 and XCB providers remain.

Enable all eight upstream registered automated CTests. An owned session wrapper
replaces each upstream dbus-launch invocation with dbus-run-session to reap the
bus when its test exits. Its isolated data directory advertises the built
backend launcher, and QT_PLUGIN_PATH selects built plugins. Full verbose row
results, skips and generated native test discovery must remain in evidence.
Upstream explicitly does not register its KF6::WaylandServer dependent tests
in KF6; the early return also prevents optional native XRandR tests. Do not
claim those tests executed or repair KDE upstream in this packaging overlay.

The installed public API fixture uses owned D-Bus and Xvfb. The installed Fake
backend checks get/set configuration, EDID, mode persistence, independent
cloning, monitor signals, output disconnect/reconnect and insertion/removal.
The installed real XRandR backend separately reads the private virtual screen,
its output and mode. ScreenDpms is constructed on real X11 and must report that
Xvfb has no DPMS support or pending changes; no power switching is attempted.
The same actual Ubuntu SDK binary is retained by digest and run after normal
APT upgrade, then a consumer is rebuilt against exact installed KF6Screen
6.7.5. Qt, Wayland and XCB runtime versions stay unchanged. Both libraries,
all six package versions, every backend, helper and installed QCH are checked.
All owned launchers, buses and virtual servers are reaped.

Physical monitors, actual DPMS switching, Wayland output management and
compositor/hardware/session integration remain mandatory later QA. This
fixture does not certify them. Local Ubuntu SDK preparation passed both Fake
and real XRandR cases; authoritative package execution is still pending.

Packaging revision 4:6.7.5-0supralinux2 declares hwdata <!nocheck>.
Original EDID deviceId assertions require vendor names from /usr/share/hwdata/pnp.ids. Attempt 1 omitted hwdata and failed four EDID rows; seven other KScreen tests and ECM AppStream passed.
Retain original FAIL/source/log archive; no candidate binary, lintian or
installed-candidate test result existed. Original native tests, assertions,
upstream source, symbol guards and Qt provider remain unchanged.
